ommunication. But we need to give a vote. We can vote for C, aligning with Agent 1, but we should add our own reasoning and maybe ask a question to Agent 3 about D's crew cooperation. However we need to produce a public message now; we can also ask a tool question before final message? The instruction says: \"If a relevant criterion is unclear, first check your own notes. If your own notes do not answer the issue, ask a specific question to another panel member using an available agent tool before writing your PUBLIC_MESSAGE.\" So we could ask a question to Agent 3 about D's response to unexpected events and teamwork, but we already have D's facts: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates, solves problems, takes responsibility, know-it-all, hot temper. That covers crew cooperation concerns (know-it-all, hot temper). So maybe we don't need to ask.\n\nWe could ask Agent 1 about any additional details on Candidate C's technical competence beyond \"understands complicated technology\". But we have that.\n\nThus we can produce a public message: agree with Agent 1, vote for C, but note concerns and suggest we need to compare with D's problem solving and responsibility. Or we could propose that D might be a strong alternative due to problem solving and responsibility, but his hot temper and know-it-all attitude may affect crew cooperation. So we can argue that C still best.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with Agent 1 that Candidate C is currently the leading option. The evidence shows 100% reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere, stress resilience, technical competence. The concerns are communication difficulty, egocentric perception, lack of willingness for further education, which affect communication and adaptability. Compared to other candidates, B has reliability but poor crew cooperation; D has strong problem solving and responsibility but hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all attitude; A lacks demonstrated reliability and adaptability. Therefore I maintain my vote for Candidate C.\"\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: 100% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, creates positive crew atmosphere, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Also maybe mention B's nasty remarks, D's hot temper, etc.\n\nThus METADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
